   "subject": "zero-order correlations in lavaan",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi, <div><br></div><div>I&#39;m very new to lavaan, and trying to figure out how to get the zero-order correlations for my model, akin to the TECH4 output from MPlus. I apologize if this question has been answered elsewhere - I searched both online and also within the group&#39;s history and wasn&#39;t able to find anything. I&#39;m guessing it&#39;s one of the outputs from <i>inspect(fit, what = &quot;std&quot;)</i>, but am having a hard time identifying the right one.</div><div><br></div><div>Thanks in advance for the help,</div><div><br></div><div>Elizabeth </div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "5VuuiyHOCwAJ",
   "from": "Terrence Jorgensen",
   "author": "3fe90052fbf2f899",
   "date": "2020-01-17T10:48:16Z",
   "subject": "Re: zero-order correlations in lavaan",
   "parts": [
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>how to get the zero-order correlations for my model</div></div></blockquote><div><br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Correlations of what?  </div><div><br></div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">cov2cor</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lavInspect</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">fit</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;sampstat&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\">$cov</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#800\"># observed correlations (estimated if using FIML)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">## model-implied correlations: </span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>lavInspect</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">fit</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;cor.ov&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#800\"># among observed variables</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>lavInspect</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">fit</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;<a href=\"http://cor.lv\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://cor.lv&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792422510252000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2E1vSryu_D3EsnE7rBRBcp\">cor.lv</a>&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#800\"># among latent variables</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>lavInspect</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">fit</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;cor.all&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#800\"># among observed and latent variables</span></div></code></div><div><div><div><div><br></div><div>See the<font face=\"courier new, monospace\"> ?lavInspect </font>help page.</div></div></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>I&#39;m guessing it&#39;s one of the outputs from <i>inspect(fit, what = &quot;std&quot;)</i>,</div></div></blockquote><div><br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>No, that is the standardized solution.  If you want to know the correlation matrix of residuals among your model&#39;s endogenous variables, you can use<font face=\"courier new, monospace\"> cov2cor(lavInspect(fit, &quot;theta&quot;))</font></div><div><br></div><div>Or likewise the residual correlation matrix of latent variables</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">cov2cor</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lavInspect</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">fit</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;std&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\">$psi</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></div></code></div><br></div><div><br></div><div><div><div>Terrence D. Jorgensen</div><div>Assistant Professor, Methods and Statistics</div><div>Research Institute for Child Development and Education, the University of Amsterdam</div><div><a href=\"http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792422510252000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2cT3w5z1lBA0VuLYClJdkX\">http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen</a></div></div><div><br></div><div></div></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  }
 ]
